{"id": 6453, "date": "2025-11-08T15:08:24", "date_gmt": "2025-11-08T07:08:24", "guid": {"rendered": "https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/?p=6453"}, "modified": "2025-11-11T15:18:33", "modified_gmt": "2025-11-11T07:18:33", "slug": "dti-seizes-%e2%82%b1229k-worth-of-unsafe-christmas-lights-in-divisoria-crackdown", "status": "publish", "type": "post", "link": "https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/press-release/dti-seizes-%e2%82%b1229k-worth-of-unsafe-christmas-lights-in-divisoria-crackdown/", "title": {"rendered": "DTI seizes ₱229K worth of unsafe Christmas lights in Divisoria crackdown"}, "content": {"rendered": "<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-fusion600 wp-image-6454\" src=\"https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/PR-Photo-DTI-warns-against-substandard-Christmas-lights.png\" alt=\"\" /></p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) confiscated more than ₱200,000 worth of uncertified and substandard Christmas lights in Divisoria. This is part of the intensified nationwide enforcement aligned with President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr.’s directive to safeguard consumers and ensure product safety this holiday season.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The items, confiscated on November 5 from five of the 35 inspected establishments, were found without the mandatory Philippine Standard (PS) and Import Commodity Clearance (ICC) markings, as well as proper labelling.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The absence of these markings is a clear violation of Department Administrative Order (DAO) No. 02, Series of 2007, which mandates all manufacturers, distributors, retailers, and importers of Christmas lights to secure certification from the Bureau of Philippine Standards (BPS) before these products are sold in the market.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The DTI–Fair Trade Enforcement Bureau (FTEB), which led the crackdown, reiterated the importance of buying only certified products to avoid fire and electrical hazards.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">“As we prepare for the holidays, let’s remain vigilant and ensure we do not compromise the safety of our homes and families by purchasing cheap or substandard Christmas lights. <i>Maging mapanuri at huwag magpaloko sa mura</i>,” FTEB said.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">FTEB also warned sellers against violating safety standards: “For businesses, let this serve as a reminder to comply with the Philippine National Standards and all relevant requirements to protect consumer welfare and market integrity.”</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Since early October, DTI’s E-Kalasag Project has inspected physical stores and online platforms nationwide, confirming 72 compliant establishments and recommending 218 violative online listings for takedown.</p>\n<p class=\"x_elementToProof\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The DTI urges both consumers and businesses to be vigilant and compliant this Christmas season to ensure a safe and bright celebration for all. <b><i>END</i></b></p>\n<p><strong>Date of Release: 08 November 2025</strong></p>\n", "protected": false}, "excerpt": {"rendered": "<p>The Department of Trade and Industry (DTI) confiscated more than  &#8230;</p>\n", "protected": false}, "author": 13, "featured_media": 6456, "comment_status": "closed", "ping_status": "closed", "sticky": false, "template": "", "format": "standard", "meta": {"footnotes": ""}, "categories": [173, 23], "tags": [], "class_list": ["post-6453", "post", "type-post", "status-publish", "format-standard", "has-post-thumbnail", "hentry", "category-photo-release", "category-press-release"], "_links": {"self": [{"href": "https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/wp-json/wp/v2/posts/6453", "targetHints": {"allow": ["GET"]}}], "collection": [{"href": "https://fairtrade.dti.gov.ph/wp-json/wp/v2/pos